# Project
This repository implements a NitroGen download → HunyuanVideo LoRA fine-tuning → video generation → offline evaluation pipeline for action-conditioned game world modeling.

# Goals
- Build a clean and reproducible pipeline
- Prefer simple, testable modules over clever abstractions
- Keep data contract stable across scripts
- Make all experiments configurable

# Commands
- Use Python 3.12
- Prefer `python -m` execution when possible
- Run `pytest` after major changes when tests exist
- Keep scripts runnable from the repo root

# Code style
- Use type hints everywhere
- Use dataclasses or pydantic-style schemas for dataset records where appropriate
- Add docstrings to all public classes and functions
- Do not hardcode paths; use config files
- Separate data logic, training logic, and evaluation logic

# Workflow
- Before writing code, check whether a schema or config file already defines the interface
- When adding a new module, add a minimal test if the repo keeps a `tests/` suite
- Prefer small commits and small code generation tasks
- When uncertain, propose file-by-file changes instead of rewriting the whole codebase

# Project structure
- Data logic goes in `src/data`
- Model wrappers go in `src/model`
- Training logic goes in `src/train`
- Evaluation logic goes in `src/eval`
- CLI scripts go in `scripts`
- Specs and planning docs go in `docs`
